# AI Coding Assistant Rules (.cursorrules)

You are an expert Frontend Engineer working on the **Sport Pro** elite performance gear project. You MUST strictly adhere to the following rules when creating, modifying, or reviewing any code.

---

## 1. Taste Design & Premium Aesthetics (Strict)

This project strictly follows the **Taste Design System** to create premium, high-agency, and visually stunning interfaces. Avoid generic "AI-style" designs (AI slop).
- **Core Guideline**: Read and apply all principles defined in [taste-design SKILL.md](file:///d:/WorkWithCorn/sport_pro_fe/skills/taste-design/SKILL.md).
- **Color Palette Constraints**:
  - Never use pure black (`#000000`) on dark themes or text. Use off-black/charcoal/zinc-950 (e.g., `#18181B`).
  - Use maximum 1 active accent color with saturation under 80% (no aggressive neon).
  - The "AI Neon Purple/Blue" glowing buttons and glowing outer rings are **strictly banned**.
  - All shadows must be whisper-soft, diffused, and slightly tinted to the background hue.
- **Typography Architecture**:
  - Avoid using `Inter` for creative or headline text. Use high-personality fonts (e.g., `Outfit`, `Geist`, `Satoshi`).
  - Body text must have relaxed leading (line-height) and never exceed `65ch` (65 characters per line).
  - Serif fonts are **strictly banned** inside dashboards or management portals.
- **Layout & Spacing**:
  - Avoid centered Hero sections when variance is high. Use asymmetric splits or left-aligned layouts.
  - The classic "3 equal cards horizontally" is banned. Use offset grids, asymmetric columns, zig-zags, or clean spacing dividers.
  - All vertical spacing must scale using `clamp()` (e.g., `clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem)`).
- **Motion & Interaction**:
  - All animations and interactive states must use heavy spring physics (e.g., `stiffness: 100, damping: 20`). Linear or uniform easing is banned.
  - Animate exclusively hardware-accelerated attributes (`transform` and `opacity`). Never animate `top`, `left`, `width`, or `height`.

---

## 2. Coding Principles & Quality (TypeScript, Next.js)

- **Separation of Concerns**: Keep components highly modular. Never put complex state machine logic or large event handler structures directly in visual files. Triage all business logic into custom hooks (`src/hooks/`).
- **Shadcn UI Approach**: Component source files reside inside `components/ui/` so you can customize and edit them. Use the `cn()` utility safely.
- **No Invents**: Banned generating placeholder data ("John Doe", "Acme") or fake/invented statistics ("99.9% Uptime", "124ms response"). If real data is not supplied, use clear placeholder indicators (e.g., `[metric]`).
- **Refer to Detailed Document**: Follow [FE_CODING_PRINCIPLES.md](file:///d:/WorkWithCorn/sport_pro_fe/docs/FE_CODING_PRINCIPLES.md).

---

## 3. Bilingual Dictionary & i18n (Mandatory)

This is a bilingual-by-default English-Vietnamese platform. **Inline translation ternaries are strictly banned in TSX files.**
- **NO INLINE TERNARIES**: Never code `locale === "vi" ? "Tiếng Việt" : "English"` in a component file.
- **Single Source of Truth**: All text, toast alerts, prompts, tooltips, dialogs, and button labels must be defined inside the translation dictionary files:
  - Vietnamese: [vi.json](file:///d:/WorkWithCorn/sport_pro_fe/src/dictionaries/vi.json)
  - English: [en.json](file:///d:/WorkWithCorn/sport_pro_fe/src/dictionaries/en.json)
- Retrieve text exclusively using the `t("key")` utility (from `useTranslation()` custom hook).
